+# THE NOTE GRID (SEQ > STEPS on a note track): knob 1 the step, knob 2 the note (C-1 to G9, starts on C4),
+# a tap on a step key puts the knob's note in that step or takes it out; a second note on a step is a chord.
+wait 300
+clear 1
+wait 300
+press SEQ
+release SEQ
+wait 300
+expect page STEPS
+expect steps 1 0
+# C4 in step 1
+tapkey 0
+wait 100
+expect stepnote 1 1 60
+expect steps 1 1
+# knob 2 up four: E4 into step 2, and into step 1 too (a chord of two)
+turn K2 4
+tapkey 2
+wait 100
+expect stepnote 1 2 64
+tapkey 0
+wait 100
+expect stepnotes 1 1 2
+expect stepnote 1 1 60
+# E4 out of step 1 again: back to one note
+tapkey 0
+wait 100
+expect stepnotes 1 1 1
+# C4 out of step 1: the step is off
+turn K2 -4
+tapkey 0
+wait 100
+expect steps 1 1
+expect stepnote 1 1 -1
+# knob 1 moves across the steps, knob 2 clamps at the ends of the keyboard
+turn K1 5
+wait 100
+expect stepcur 6
+turn K2 -100
+turn K2 -100
+turn K2 200
+turn K2 200
+tapkey 4
+wait 100
+expect stepnote 1 3 127
+# velocity and length are knobs 4 and 3 of the same page
+turn K1 -10
+turn K1 2
+wait 60
+turn K4 -1
+wait 60
+expect stepvel 1 3 99
+# OCT+ and OCT- turn the 16-step pages, and the knobs go to the page's first step
+settp 1 LENGTH 40
+wait 100
+press OCT+
+release OCT+
+wait 100
+expect stepcur 17
+press OCT+
+release OCT+
+wait 100
+expect stepcur 33
+press OCT-
+release OCT-
+wait 100
+expect stepcur 17
